{
  "topic": "How to move an asteroid: DART and Hera",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "Can We Move an Asteroid? The Mission That Did It ☄️",
  "hook": "What if an asteroid were heading straight for Earth? Could we push it out of the way?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "din_asteroid",
      "narration": "What if an asteroid were heading straight for Earth? Could we push it out of the way?",
      "on_screen_text": "Can we move an asteroid?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "move"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "din_impact",
      "narration": "It sounds like a movie, but it has happened before: sixty-six million years ago, a rock about ten kilometers wide changed the history of life.",
      "on_screen_text": "It happened before",
      "highlight_words": [
        "happened"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "din_crater",
      "narration": "It left a giant crater in what is now Mexico, called Chicxulub, and wiped out the big dinosaurs.",
      "on_screen_text": "The Chicxulub crater",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Chicxulub"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_dart",
      "narration": "The big news is that humanity has already pushed an asteroid on purpose. I'm Leo, and today I'll tell you how we did it.",
      "on_screen_text": "We already pushed one",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pushed"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_belt",
      "narration": "Let's start at the beginning. The solar system is full of rocks left over from when the planets formed.",
      "on_screen_text": "Leftover rocks",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Leftover"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Wandering rocks"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_belt",
      "narration": "Most of them circle far away, in the asteroid belt, between Mars and Jupiter.",
      "on_screen_text": "The asteroid belt",
      "highlight_words": [
        "belt"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_watch",
      "narration": "But some have orbits that pass near ours. Astronomers search for them and track them every night.",
      "on_screen_text": "Some pass close by",
      "highlight_words": [
        "close"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_safe",
      "narration": "The good news: almost all the big ones, over a kilometer wide, have already been found, and none we know of will hit us anytime soon.",
      "on_screen_text": "The big ones are tracked",
      "highlight_words": [
        "tracked"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "din_impact",
      "narration": "The problem is the medium ones, the size of a stadium: there are many more, and they're harder to spot.",
      "on_screen_text": "Medium ones are the worry",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Medium"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_binary",
      "narration": "To test whether we can deflect one, NASA picked a pair of asteroids: Didymos and its little moon, Dimorphos.",
      "on_screen_text": "Didymos and Dimorphos",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Dimorphos"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "DART's punch"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_binary",
      "narration": "It was the perfect target: it poses no threat to Earth, and from here we could measure how long the moon takes to go around.",
      "on_screen_text": "The perfect target",
      "highlight_words": [
        "perfect"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "coh_hook",
      "narration": "In November 2021, the DART spacecraft launched, roughly the size of a small car, not counting its solar panels.",
      "on_screen_text": "DART launches",
      "highlight_words": [
        "DART"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_dart",
      "narration": "Ten months later, in September 2022, it slammed into Dimorphos at more than six kilometers per second.",
      "on_screen_text": "Impact!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Impact!"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_dart",
      "narration": "It carried no explosives: the crash itself was the push, like one billiard ball hitting another.",
      "on_screen_text": "Like billiards",
      "highlight_words": [
        "billiards"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_shrink",
      "narration": "Before, Dimorphos took almost twelve hours to circle Didymos. After the hit, it took about thirty-three minutes less.",
      "on_screen_text": "33 minutes shorter",
      "highlight_words": [
        "33"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_shrink",
      "narration": "That was more than expected, because the crash threw out a huge cloud of rocks and dust that added an extra push.",
      "on_screen_text": "More than expected",
      "highlight_words": [
        "expected"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_hera",
      "narration": "And now comes the new part. Europe's Hera spacecraft, launched in 2024, has just arrived at those asteroids.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hera arrives",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Hera"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "Hera arrives"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_hera",
      "narration": "It's like returning to the scene of the crash. Hera will measure the crater, the mass of Dimorphos and how much its shape changed.",
      "on_screen_text": "Back to the scene",
      "highlight_words": [
        "scene"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_hera",
      "narration": "It also carries two mini-satellites, about the size of a shoebox, that will get even closer.",
      "on_screen_text": "Two mini-satellites",
      "highlight_words": [
        "mini-satellites"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_binary",
      "narration": "With that data we'll know how much force it really takes to move a rock, not just in a computer.",
      "on_screen_text": "Real data",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Real"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_deflect",
      "narration": "So how would all this protect us? The secret isn't strength, it's time.",
      "on_screen_text": "The secret is time",
      "highlight_words": [
        "time"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How we stay safe"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_deflect",
      "narration": "A tiny nudge, given years ahead, changes the rock's orbit just a little.",
      "on_screen_text": "A tiny nudge",
      "highlight_words": [
        "tiny"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_deflect",
      "narration": "Over time, that little bit adds up to thousands of kilometers, and the rock sails past.",
      "on_screen_text": "And it misses",
      "highlight_words": [
        "misses"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_watch",
      "narration": "That's why finding them early matters most. The Vera Rubin Observatory in Chile is already scanning the whole southern sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "Find them early",
      "highlight_words": [
        "early"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_safe",
      "narration": "And it's not the only mission: Japan and NASA have already brought back pieces of two asteroids, Ryugu and Bennu.",
      "on_screen_text": "Asteroid samples",
      "highlight_words": [
        "samples"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_orbit",
      "narration": "Surprise: some asteroids put on a show for us. Dust from one called Phaethon creates the Geminid meteor shower every December.",
      "on_screen_text": "An asteroid of shooting stars",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shooting"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_rain",
      "narration": "This year its best night is December thirteenth to fourteenth. Find a dark sky and look up.",
      "on_screen_text": "December 13–14",
      "highlight_words": [
        "December"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "met_burn",
      "narration": "Each grain enters the atmosphere so fast that the air around it glows, and that's a shooting star.",
      "on_screen_text": "That's a shooting star",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shooting"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_watch",
      "narration": "So, for the first time in history, a species on this planet has learned to defend itself from rocks in the sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "We learned to defend ourselves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "defend"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ast_outro",
      "narration": "Which space mission should we explain next? Tell me in the comments.",
      "on_screen_text": "Which mission is next?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "mission"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "Humanity has already pushed an asteroid on purpose. Here's what the DART spacecraft did, what the Hera mission is finding now, and how we'd protect ourselves from a space rock. Original 3D animation; sizes and distances are not to scale.",
